Subject: [PATCH 3/3] QuickTTY managed launch, reader EOF and bounded terminal tail
Origin: QuickTTY local fix (not an upstream backport)
Base-Commit: f9a3f24a56bf05f70894e1a084809d4fffadf420 (1.3.2-dev, after patches 0002-0003)

Add explicit managed-only helper launch and atomic reader completion state.
The Zig 0.16 reader pipeline publishes COMPLETE only after the gather stage
proves PTY EOF and the parse stage drains every published batch. Cancellation,
unconfirmed HUP, setup failure, and teardown fail closed. Read the current
bounded terminal tail under the renderer lock with bounded suffix storage.
Preserve normal launch behavior and existing public C layouts. New
quicktty-prefixed exports are private to this embedding integration.
Ghostty MIT license applies. Native compilation and package-symbol validation
have passed; runtime verification remains outstanding.

